Description: LOSK - Linux On-Screen Keyboard
 A compact on-screen keyboard for Linux, laid out like a normal desktop
 keyboard rather than a tablet keyboard. Includes function keys, a full
 navigation cluster, arrows and a real numeric keypad.
 .
 Typing is done through the kernel uinput device, so it works with any
 application. Word suggestions are fully offline and learn the words you
 use most.
 .
 Made by ZeshMC.
